  "notes": "West leads the ♠J against 6♥. West's spade opening lead is won by South. The only possible problem is a 4-0 trump break. If West has all 4 hearts, South can easily succeed unless the ♥A is cashed on the first round.\n\nIf East has all 4 hearts, the first round will have to be played from the dummy and a trump endplay will be needed. To preserve both options, South should cross in diamonds and lead the ♥8 or ♥7 from dummy.\n\nIf East discards, South can win the ♥K and easily hold West to 1 trump trick. If East follows with the ♥6, South plays low from the closed hand, holding East to 1 trump trick.\n\nIf East follows with a higher heart, South wins the ♥K. West's discard means a trump endplay will be needed. To prepare for the trump endplay, South must cash all of his side winners and take a ruff in the closed hand.\n\nEast will have to have 3 spades, at least 2 diamonds, and at least 3 clubs. South should start by cashing 3 rounds of clubs. When West discards on the third round, East will have to be 3424 for the contract to have a chance.\n\nSouth crosses in diamonds and plays dummy's fourth club, ruffing. After South cashes his top spades, South, North, and East are all down to 3 trumps. A trump is played and ducked in dummy. East will win, but is held to 1 trump trick.",
  "commentary_paragraphs": [
    "West leads the ♠J against 6♥. West's spade opening lead is won by South. The only possible problem is a 4-0 trump break. If West has all 4 hearts, South can easily succeed unless the ♥A is cashed on the first round.",
    "If East has all 4 hearts, the first round will have to be played from the dummy and a trump endplay will be needed. To preserve both options, South should cross in diamonds and lead the ♥8 or ♥7 from dummy.",
    "If East discards, South can win the ♥K and easily hold West to 1 trump trick. If East follows with the ♥6, South plays low from the closed hand, holding East to 1 trump trick.",
    "If East follows with a higher heart, South wins the ♥K. West's discard means a trump endplay will be needed. To prepare for the trump endplay, South must cash all of his side winners and take a ruff in the closed hand.",
    "East will have to have 3 spades, at least 2 diamonds, and at least 3 clubs. South should start by cashing 3 rounds of clubs. When West discards on the third round, East will have to be 3424 for the contract to have a chance.",
    "South crosses in diamonds and plays dummy's fourth club, ruffing. After South cashes his top spades, South, North, and East are all down to 3 trumps. A trump is played and ducked in dummy. East will win, but is held to 1 trump trick."
  ],
